# /onboarding is NOT here any more — it proxies to the MMS app, in netlify.toml with the
# other portal routes. Rules in this file would win over that proxy and serve the old
# static page instead, so the entry stays deleted rather than commented back in.
/onboarding-form  /onboarding  301
/welcome        /welcome.html     200

# "Our Tutors" moved off /tutors, one character away from /tutor — the MMS tutor PORTAL,
# which netlify.toml proxies to Vercel. Two different audiences (a parent browsing who we
# are, versus a tutor signing in to work) separated by a single letter, and nothing on
# either page said which one you were on.
#
# Both forms 301 rather than 200: the old path is in Google's index and on whatever anyone
# has bookmarked or linked, so it has to keep resolving — but it should hand the visitor
# the new address rather than silently serve the page under a name we are retiring.
/tutors         /our-tutors  301
/tutors.html    /our-tutors  301
